Verdict: MINOR
Findings:
- [minor] Markdown table-cell rendering hazard on line 260 and line 279 — both cells contain ``` `present | partial | missing | not-applicable` ``` with unescaped pipes inside inline code inside a pipe table. GitHub's GFM renderer treats unescaped `|` as cell delimiters even inside backticks, so the "TDD Test List" row and the status-values acceptance criterion will likely render with extra columns. The content is correct; the delivery format is not. Change to `\|` inside the code span or replace with commas, e.g. ``` `present`, `partial`, `missing`, `not-applicable` ```.
- [minor] Tier-1 scope coupling is only narrative — `test_tier1_checklist_covers_all_scope_repos` (line 257) hardcodes the four repo names instead of parsing `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`. The plan asserts BUSINESS_BRAIN is "the authority" (L34) but the test treats it as a static snapshot. If BUSINESS_BRAIN's Tier-1 section ever changes, the checklist won't drift-detect. Either parse the table in the test or add a separate assertion that the checklist's repo set equals the parsed Tier-1 list from BUSINESS_BRAIN.md.
- [minor] "Multiple concrete banned-pattern signatures" is unquantified — L216, L252, L273 all say "multiple" without a minimum. Prior review rounds specifically patched this from a "token example" to "multiple"; two placeholder strings would technically satisfy. Quantify (`≥3 distinct categories such as literal legacy filenames, legacy path fragments, and legacy reference blocks used as navigation authority`) to make the guard auditable.
- [minor] Artifact Map row bleeds scope — L142 lists an "Optional script/docs drift follow-up only (not in this issue)" inside the scope-defining Artifact Map. That row belongs in "Risks and Open Questions" or a new "Not in scope" section; leaving it in the artifact map dilutes what the issue ships.
- [minor] `test_tier1_contract_links_child_issues` under-specifies placement — L253 only requires `#2461`–`#2465` be textually present; a stray paragraph could satisfy it. Strengthen by requiring each issue number appear alongside its scope clause (e.g., `#2465` inside the freshness section, `#2461` linked to assetutilities in the checklist rows, etc.), especially since L254 already enforces `#2465`'s section-level placement — the pattern should extend to the others.

Checks performed:
- Verified `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` L16–22 names exactly the four tier-1 repos the plan cites; confirmed `assethold` is listed under a different tier (L37), so the plan's rationale for retiring older starter-repo examples is sourced.
