- Verified `docs/plans/README.md` L278 already has the `#2460` index row (acceptance criterion L282 is therefore satisfiable without further edits to the row format).
- Traced the scorecard negative-authority sentence through pseudocode (L181/L194), asserts (L215/L218), tests (L256/L259), acceptance (L275/L278) — identical wording, dual-surface enforcement confirmed.
- Traced TDD sequencing: pseudocode `implement_with_tdd()` L197–202 (write test → confirm failure → edit contract → edit checklist → rerun), assert L220, test `test_tdd_sequence_requires_tests_fail_before_doc_edits` L261, acceptance L280 — explicit and four-way-consistent.
- Traced bulk-artifact-store wording: deliverable L151 defines the universal rule and demotes `/mnt/ace/data`; pseudocode L182–185 restates the three-part structure; tests L250 assert rule+definition+example; acceptance L271 repeats all three — consistent, no residual literal-path-first phrasing detected.
- Re-read L289–307 Adversarial Review Summary: historical MAJOR/MAJOR/MINOR verdicts are now labeled historical, current draft self-labels "PENDING RE-REVIEW", which matches the rerun instruction in the review target.
